menu "ai_engine"

    choice AI_ENGINE_COMMAND_BACKEND
        prompt "command backend (KEHOACH 3.12, ADR-0012)"
        default AI_ENGINE_COMMAND_BACKEND_KWS
        help
            Which command directory builds into ai_engine; the model image names its command entries after it.

        config AI_ENGINE_COMMAND_BACKEND_KWS
            bool "kws: src/command/, a neutral shell until E11-T17 runs its net"

        config AI_ENGINE_COMMAND_BACKEND_CTC
            bool "ctc: src/command_ctc/, the streaming encoder and the constrained CTC decision"

        config AI_ENGINE_COMMAND_BACKEND_RNNT
            bool "rnnt: src/command_rnnt/, the ctc encoder with a predictor and a joiner, every command scored exactly"
    endchoice

    choice AI_ENGINE_CORES
        prompt "cores ai_engine's own ops run on (KEHOACH 5.1, ADR-0027)"
        default AI_ENGINE_CORES_ONE
        help
            Which src/core/espdl/runtime/espdl_split_*.cpp builds into ai_engine. With two, main creates phu_task
            on core 1 at priority 1, below thu and sach, and the ops that split hand it half their work.

        config AI_ENGINE_CORES_ONE
            bool "one: every op runs whole on the task running its network"

        config AI_ENGINE_CORES_TWO
            bool "two: each op runs half on the network's task and half on phu_task on core 1"
    endchoice

    config AI_ENGINE_LOAN_RESERVE_BYTES
        int "internal RAM the ops' loan leaves free (KEHOACH 6.5, ADR-0025)"
        default 0
        range 0 65536
        help
            Each run lends ai_engine's own ops the largest free internal block, at most what they asked for, less
            this many bytes, which other tasks may still allocate while the graph runs. None by default: the other
            tasks allocate from the rest of internal RAM, and an op whose weights miss the loan reads them from flash.

endmenu
